{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3FWStzruKdHRW61U7T2","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed or committed anything. A per-day breakdown can't go into `out/summary.csv` without breaking the portal file.\n\n**The problem:** the README says `out/summary.csv` must stay under 50 lines and that the portal silently drops anything beyond that. The 2025 data covers 248 distinct days. Putting those daily rows in this file would make it about 260 lines, so the partner would get the first ~49 rows (roughly January to February) with no error on either side. They would have no way of knowing the rest was missing.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Separate daily file (my recommendation):** add a new file, e.g. `out/summary_daily.csv` with `period,total,count`, written by `scripts/summarize.py`. `out/summary.csv` stays monthly and within the limit. This only works if the partner can pull a second file from the portal, and I don't know whether they can.\n2. **Ask the partner or portal owner** whether the 50-line limit can be raised. Until it is, per-day rows can't go in this file safely.\n3. **Something coarser that fits,** e.g. weekly totals: 53 weeks also breaks the limit, so this would only work for part of the year.\n\nTell me which one, and if it's option 1, whether the partner can actually get the new file.\n\n**Separate thing I noticed:** `out/summary.csv` has 11 months and is missing 2025-12, which I committed earlier. It looks like `summarize.py` hasn't been run since then. Regenerating it is safe, since it adds just one row, but I've left it for you to decide.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":126,"cache_read_input_tokens":19850,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":126,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-72>","timestamp":"2026-11-14T17:55:54.396Z","request_id":"gen-1794678946-eJzVQGWYsVXcr6irXAXl"}
